From: Sam <sam@bristolwireless.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:03:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] AP_WheelEncoder: add Hiwonder EMM backend

Expose the EMM encoder totals as WENC_TYPE 11 so Rover feeds them to EKF3
as wheel odometry (EK3_SRCn_VELXY 7). WENC instance 0 reads EMM encoder 1,
instance 1 reads EMM encoder 2.

AP_HiwonderEMM now reads the encoders every 50Hz tick instead of every 5th
(ADC stays at 10Hz) and stamps each read. Rover sends a zero angle change
between fresh samples, so the old 10Hz read would have looked like standstill
to EKF3 for four of every five updates.

The backend starts distance at zero on the first reading, because the EMM
keeps its totals while powered.

Known gap: if the EMM stops answering, Rover keeps sending zero angle
changes with a growing time base. EKF3 then sees a stopped wheel. The pre-arm
check only covers the start of a run.

AI-assisted (Claude). SITL Rover build only (AP_HIWONDEREMM_ENABLED=1 via
CXXFLAGS), not run, not tested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RyNKbZ8zczCSQUp1aaUSKQ
